SUMMARY:Introduction to 3D Printing
DESCRIPTION:Learn how 3D printers work and how you can print at the Toronto Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This class includes hands-on instruction with Prusa Slicer\, the software used to prepare your 3D object file for printing on a Prusa MK3S+ 3D printer. \nThis class is for those who are interested in learning more about 3D printing and how to use the Prusa software. Computers will be provided. \nRegistration opens April 9 at 9:00 am. Register online at https://tpl.ca/locations/DA/\, in person at the front desk\, or by calling the branch at 416-393-7783.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/introduction-to-3d-printing/
LOCATION:Danforth Coxwell Library\, 1675 Danforth Avenue\, Toronto\, M4C 5P2
ORGANIZER;CN="Danforth Coxwell Branch%2C Toronto Public Library":MAILTO:dastaff@tpl.ca
END:VEVENT
